COMPILATION OF: E46N17

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46N17

   1 a 0000 E46N17:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2c] CREATE's OWN TAIL, spelled out.  Line 39
   4 a 0006      is the six-item list P2b lowered ([C296]); 41, 44 and
   5 a 0006      45 are the three SKIP statements P2c needs.  CREATE
   6 a 0006      opens with a VARIABLE title, which is why a corpus
   7 a 0006      program cannot be a specimen; here the title is a
   8 a 0006      literal and the record layout is CREATE's, so this
   9 a 0006      object is the byte witness for CREATE:39-45 without
  10 a 0006      needing CREATE's own bytes. */
  11 c 0006   dcl outf file;
  12 c 0006   dcl name char(30) varying, addr char(30) varying,
  13 c 0006         city char(20) varying, state char(10) varying,
  14 c 0006         zip  fixed dec(6), phone char(12) varying;
  15 c 0006   open file(outf) stream output title('N17OUT DAT');
  16 c 0023   /* the title length is 10, matching the model's DATA */
  17 c 0023   put file(outf) list(name,addr,city,state,zip,phone);
  18 c 0071   put file(outf) skip;
  19 c 0085   put file(outf) skip list('EOF');
  20 c 00A4   put file(outf) skip;
  21 c 00B8   close file(outf);
  22 a 00BE end E46N17;

CODE SIZE = 00C1
DATA AREA = 007C
FREE SYMS = 3841
END  COMPILATION
